  "startedAt": "2026-10-13T09:44:24.281Z",
  "steps": [
    "In an empty project the new recipe entry opens guidance, offers no invented actor, disables Create, and writes no author data.",
    "The ordinary World GUI creates an OC and then a compatible RPG player projection with size 72×88, speed 180 and blue color. Its source relationship points to that OC; no fixture author objects are injected.",
    "Horizontal, vertical and two-column grid previews show every old/new position without changing row fields, reviewed recipe JSON, editor state or author files. Explicit Apply changes only all positions and invalidates JSON review; Undo restores exact raw coordinates including 0140.00 and 1.8e2. Actor order, UUIDs, object references and inheritance remain unchanged.",
    "Editing an actor coordinate invalidates both pending layout and prior Undo; adding/removing rows also invalidates stale layout authority, and disabled actions cannot overwrite later edits. An unfinished minus coordinate and a row whose later positions would exceed the coordinate bound reject the entire layout without modifying any row or author file.",
    "Switching actors and changing Chinese/English/Japanese preserves the pending grid preview and every raw field. At 390px the settings, preview/apply action and fixed header/footer remain reachable without horizontal overflow. Cancelling still creates no author file, registration or editor draft.",
    "The explicitly applied grid transfers all three reviewed rows to one ordinary unsaved JSON draft; ordinary Save persists the exact bytes and one registration. Both projection actors remain symbolic inheritance declarations, while the plain OC retains explicit baseline fields. Earlier OC/projection bytes stay unchanged.",
    "Saved preview resolves both references independently to the same inherited 72×88, blue, speed-180 projection. Materialization preserves all three UUIDs, author order and individual coordinates, keeping inherited fields unflattened. It creates only an independent Scene2D and its registration.",
    "Real Godot plan/build/headless execution succeeds with three distinct scene identities. The two projection instances each move 45px and the plain actor moves 40px under the shared arrow-input step, preserving the applied grid starts [100,120], [250,120], [100,220]. Plan/build/run change no author bytes. This checks repeated definitions and distinct runtime instances, not independently routed control bindings."
  ],
